{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Upon his two officers</b>. These two officials were both eunuchs, for the officers of the cupbearers and the bakers were also in the king's harem, and the kings would castrate them. But the view of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 40:2) is that סָרִיסִים means officers and grandees: he rendered in Potiphar (Onkelos on Genesis 37:36) רַבָּא דְּפַרְעֹה and here עַל תְּרֵין רַבְרְבָנוֹהִי, and so Jonathan translated (II Kings 20:18) וְהָיוּ סָרִיסִים בְּהֵיכַל מֶלֶךְ בָּבֶל."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The citation from II Kings 20:18 is attributed to Jonathan (Targum), but the verse is biblical; the reference is to the Aramaic rendering of that verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:08.840046002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}